Paragraph  cuisine_focus_text": "[17] extended the k-regret minimizing notion to nonlinear functions. The focus of this paper is designing efficient algorithms for the regret-ratio minimizing problem proposed in [22]. In two- dimensional case, compared to quadratic existing Sweeping-Line, we propose the linearithmic dynamic programming algorithm 2D- RRMS, while for the high-dimensional case we provide the lin- earithmic HD-RRMS that guarantees a user controllable distance from the optimal solution."
